        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8bbbc065-4148-5f5e-b319-ecfe4bb12fd0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Microchip Technology, Keurig Green Mountain\n- Products: PICkit, PIC microcontrollers, microcontrollers, serial EEPROM, serial SRAM, KEELOQ, RF devices, analog devices\n- People: Bob Stiller\n- Topics: semiconductors, specialty coffee, coffeemakers\n\nFacts:\n- Keurig Green Mountain was founded in 1981 and is a U.S.-headquartered specialty coffee and coffeemaker company.\n- Bob Stiller, also known as Robert P. Stiller, founded the Keurig Green Mountain coffee company in 1993.\n- Microchip Technology is an American manufacturer of microcontroller, memory, and analog semiconductors.\n- Microchip Technology products include microcontrollers such as PICmicro, dsPIC/PIC24, PIC32, AVR, AVR32, and SAM.\n- Microchip Technology products also include serial EEPROM devices, serial SRAM devices, KEELOQ devices, RF devices, thermal devices, power and battery management analog devices, and linear, interface, and mixed signal devices.\n- PICkit is a family of programmers for PIC microcontrollers made by Microchip Technology.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
